{% comment %}
  Custom robots.txt.liquid for wcsafety.com

  ⚠️  REVISED 2026-08-09 after an indexing incident. Read
      `audits/incident-2026-07-robots-block.md` before editing.

  The previous version of this file blocked:

      Disallow: /collections/*/products/
      Disallow: /collections/all/products/

  Those two lines were deployed around 2026-07-01 and caused a
  traffic loss. They are deliberately NOT in this file. Do not
  re-add them.

  Why they were harmful:
    The goal was to stop /collections/<x>/products/<slug> duplicates
    competing with the canonical /products/<slug>. But robots.txt
    does not deduplicate — it only stops crawling. A URL Google
    cannot crawl is a URL whose <link rel="canonical"> Google cannot
    read. So instead of consolidating onto /products/<slug>, the
    duplicates were stranded: Search Console reported "Indexed,
    though blocked by robots.txt" AND "Duplicate without
    user-selected canonical" in the same notice on 2026-07-03, then
    "Blocked by robots.txt" on 2026-07-28, then "Duplicate, Google
    chose different canonical than user" on 2026-08-08.

    Duplicate content is a canonical-tag problem. Fix it with
    canonicals (see `fixes/wcsafety-com/canonical-verification.md`),
    never with robots.txt.

  What this file does relative to Shopify's default:
    - Keeps every default Shopify Disallow (cart, checkout, admin,
      orders, account, policies search, etc.).
    - Blocks only Shopify's filter/sort state parameters, which are
      genuine crawl-budget waste and carry no unique content:
      _pos, _fid, _ss, sort_by, and the filter.* family.
    - Deliberately does NOT block ?page= pagination. Paginated
      collection URLs are how Googlebot discovers deeper products;
      blocking them suppresses discovery. The previous
      `Disallow: /collections/*?*` rule caught pagination as
      collateral damage.
    - Deliberately does NOT block any /products/ path, under any
      prefix. Canonicals handle those.
    - Keeps the Sitemap directive emitted by Shopify.

  Where this goes in Shopify:
    Online Store → Themes → ... → Edit code → Templates → Add a new
    template → "robots" → "liquid" → paste this file's contents.

  After deploying, verify at https://wcsafety.com/robots.txt that
  no /collections/*/products/ rule is present.
{% endcomment %}
{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent }}

  {%- for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{ rule }}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Custom additions for wcsafety.com — filter/sort state only.
    See the header comment before adding anything here.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {{ "Disallow: /collections/*?*_pos=" }}
  {{ "Disallow: /collections/*?*_fid=" }}
  {{ "Disallow: /collections/*?*_ss=" }}
  {{ "Disallow: /collections/*?*sort_by=" }}
  {{ "Disallow: /collections/*?*filter." }}

  {%- if group.sitemap != blank %}

  {{ group.sitemap }}
  {%- endif %}
{% endfor %}
